      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "One rounded box, repeated on a grid that goes on forever: the Repeat folds every point into one cell, so endless copies cost what one does. Each copy is moved, turned, shrunk and tinted by its cell and the Seed, and the Ground after the Repeat is not repeated, since a modifier changes only what is cabled into it. Try the Repeat's Seed, Scatter, Spin, Size and Tint, or Render 3D's Lens Type on Fisheye."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
